==English==
{{wp}}

===Etymology===
Borrowed from {{bor|en|es|sombrero|t=hat}}, from {{m|es|sombra|t=shadow, shade}} + {{m|es|-ero}}, literally, "shade-maker". The drink was named after the hat.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|GA}} {{IPA|en|/səmˈbɹɛɹ.oʊ/|/sɑmˈbɹɛɹ.oʊ/|/soʊmˈbɹɛɹ.oʊ/}}
** {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-sombrero.wav|Audio (Southern England)}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɛɹəʊ|s=3}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}
[[File:Sombrero (PSF).png|thumb|sombrero]]

# A kind of [[hat]] with a high conical or cylindrical crown and a saucer-shaped brim, highly embroidered, made of plush felt.
#* {{RQ:Landon Romance|page=135|volume=III|passage=Beatrice looked up and saw a man standing before her; the huge '''sombrero''' overshadowed his face, but the light of the lamp shone on a large and glittering knife in his girdle.}}
# A mixed drink with [[coffee liqueur]] and [[cream]].
# {{lb|en|bowling}} A series of four consecutive [[strike|strikes]].

